From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:19:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] WIP: ban every dbus-crate constructor, open_private
 included; HARBOUR.md for the gate fixes

clippy.toml now bans the address-taking D-Bus constructors too
(Channel::open_private, the blocking connections' new_address,
ffidisp's open_private): libdbus runs autolaunch: and unixexec:
addresses as readily as it connects to unix: ones, so only the
function that checks the address may open one. The selftest proves
each fires and that a per-site lift stays lifted. The Quick Share BLE
nudge and its test fixture lift the ban at their one call each
(CONTRACT); bluetooth/bus.rs and tests/bluetooth.rs are the
Wormhole/Bluetooth agent's, which lifts it there.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ENZSCiAud5Vs29ugEacpyR
